<p>George Armstrong Custer was born December 5, 1839, in New Rumley, Ohio, to farmer and blacksmith Emanuel Henry Custer and his second wife, Marie Ward Kirkpatrick Custer. Both parents brought children from earlier marriages. Their children together included George, Thomas, Boston, Nevin, and Margaret. Emanuel named George for minister George Armstrong in hopes that his son would enter the clergy, but George's mischievous nature and taste for alcohol led elsewhere.</p>

